On Dec 2, 4:45=A0am, "EMK" <noneofyourbusin...@columbus.rr.com> wrote:
> Okay, I'll admit that searching for hidden door, passages,
> traps, etc. has got to be one of my least favorite aspects of
> any RPG. =A0So, it's needless to say (why do people always
> preface things they're about to say with that phrase?) that
> I'm getting a bit tired of mashing my "s" key (yeah, I know I
> could type out "n9s", but it hardly seems worth it) when I get
> to a level composed of only three rooms and no down staircase.

> I've started out with a Valk since the consensus seems to be
> that their the easiest for newbs to ascend with (+3 shield,
> Excalibur, and Mjollnir are pretty handy for a low-level
> character), but I'm wondering if my mid-range INT & WIS might
> be holding me back from finding stuff as quickly as I could if
> I was playing a Priest or a Wizard. =A0Then again, there are all
> those classes with some sort of intrinsic Search ability...

> So, here are my questions:

> 1. =A0Does INT or WIS (or any other ability) have a direct
> effect on how many times I have to hit the (s)earch key to
> find things?

No, not as far as I know.  The critical thing is luck (so you
might want to trip down to the end of the mines).

> 2. =A0How exactly does the intrinsic Search ability of some
> classes work?  (e.g. Does it automatically do a free (s)earch
> each turn or maybe even "n5s" or better? =A0Does it just have a
> fixed chance of revealing anything hidden the first time you
> encounter an area?)

The first.

> 3. =A0Do items that grant a Search ability work the same way as
> the class intrinsic Search ability?

At least one that you can get early not only does an automatic s
each turn, but also increases your chances of finding something
(I think).  Carrying a luckstone and wielding Excalibur, it's
really rare to have to search much.

> 4. =A0Ditto for monster corpses that you can eat?

None that I know of.

> 5. =A0Any other way I might not have thought of that could save
> me some time/keystrokes?

Excalibur, a luckstone, then throw some gems at a co-aligned
Unicorn.  If I don't have magic protection, I'll generally
search a lot before moving---with Excalibur and good luck, I
feel fairly safe after two additional searches.

